# Optional local-dev environment for the app. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# The app reads its Lakebase connection URL from a Databricks SECRET at runtime
# (default: database/lakebase-url), via the Databricks SDK — the URL is never
# put in the environment. So to run LOCALLY you need:
#   1. Databricks auth configured (a CLI profile, or the two vars below).
#   2. The secret to already exist — run `python setup_secrets.py` once.
#
# These override the secret's scope/key if you used different names (the code
# already defaults to database / lakebase-url, so usually you can omit them):
# LAKEBASE_SECRET_SCOPE=database
# LAKEBASE_SECRET_KEY=lakebase-url
#
# Databricks auth for local dev (or use `databricks auth login`):
# DATABRICKS_HOST=https://<your-workspace>.cloud.databricks.com
# DATABRICKS_TOKEN=<personal-access-token>
